{key:'cookies',title:'Golden Eagle Oatmeal Cookies',short:'Oatmeal Cookies',category:'Desserts',img:'cookies.png',desc:'Soft, nostalgic cookies from the original recipe collection.',note:'1 cup syrup · 3 cups oats<br>nuts + raisins<br>375° · 12–15 min · 4 dozen!',ingredients:['2 sticks butter','1 cup Golden Eagle Syrup','½ cup sugar','2 eggs','1 teaspoon vanilla','2 cups flour','1 teaspoon cinnamon','¾ teaspoon baking soda','½ teaspoon salt','3 cups old-fashioned oats','1 cup chopped nuts','1 cup raisins'],instructions:'Cream butter, syrup, and sugar; mix in eggs and vanilla. Combine dry ingredients and add to mixture, then fold in oats, nuts, and raisins. Drop by teaspoons onto a baking sheet. Bake at 375°F for 12–15 minutes. Makes approximately four dozen.'}
